title: Fix dead f_lseek error checks (FRESULT is never < 0)
updated: 2026-09-29T03:45:18Z
---

f_lseek/f_read/f_write return FRESULT, a non-negative enum (FR_OK==0), so
"if (f_lseek(...) < 0)" is dead: a real seek error slips through. Introduced by the
POSIX->FatFs port (upstream lseek() returned -1).

Sites to change from "< 0" to "!= FR_OK" (keep cdb_bread(...) < 0, that returns C-style -1):
  cdb_seek.c:52, 61, 71
  cdb_make_put.c:44 (part of the f_read compound), 46, 86

Already correct, leave as reference for the right style: cdb_make.c:160 (!= 0),
cdb_make_put.c:63 zerofill (truthy).

Verify: sh t/compile-check.sh stays clean; add/adjust a behavioural error-path test
(see the harness ticket) that forces a failing f_lseek and asserts the error propagates.
Lane: tinycdbff-worker.

